# LeakSanitizer suppressions for gRParse test binaries.
#
# Use with: LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/lsan.supp and
# ASAN_OPTIONS=fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 (see the ONNX Runtime entry).
#
# ONNX Runtime makes one 14-byte allocation inside OrtApis::CreateEnv that it
# never frees: the first Ort::Env a process builds (including the failed
# loads the missing-model cases exercise) leaks it, later ones do not.
# Third-party, one-time, not per request. The release libonnxruntime.so is
# stripped, so every frame inside it is unnamed; the first named frame is
# the C++ API's inline Ort::Env constructor, compiled into our own code.
# Matching it needs the full malloc stack: run with
# ASAN_OPTIONS=fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 (the frame-pointer unwinder stops at
# the first frame inside the library, which has no frame pointers).
leak:Ort::Env::Env

# curl_global_init, which s3_client.cpp runs once per process and never
# undoes (curl_global_cleanup is not thread-safe while transfers run),
# initializes OpenSSL, whose config load leaves its error-queue state on the
# initializing thread. One-time global state inside libcurl/libcrypto.
leak:curl_global_init
